last six winners of the PEN/Bellwether Prize for Socially Engaged Fiction, for which she is also a judge. Her authors have been Alex Award winners and finalists for the National Book Award, the Dayton Literary Peace Prize, the Kirkus Prize, the Story Prize ... \",\"title\":\"https://pen.org/meet-the-2021-literary-awards-judges/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d21\"},\"ref\":\"d21\",\"snippet\":\" ... Gibb was the winner of the Trillium Book Award in 2006, a Scotiabank Giller Prize short list nominee in 2005, winner of the city of Toronto Book Award in 2000 and the recipient of the CBC Canadian Literary Award for short fiction in 2001. Her books have been ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.yorku.ca/laps/huma/canadian-writers/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d27\"},\"ref\":\"d27\",\"snippet\":\" ... Kaya and its authors have been the recipients of numerous awards, including the Gregory Kolovakas Prize for Outstanding New Literary Press, the American Book Award, the Association for Asian American Studies Book Award, the PEN Beyond Margins Open Book Prize, the Asian American Writers' Workshop Award, and the ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.clmp.org/programs-opportunities/firecracker/firecracker-awards-winners-archive/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"51e4342f78f3ccee7ba21d33c1f2dd1063bc6a8955bf4c7b524f5f75554b4c03\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"25c523eb6258be8594890cad6bf2e2c44a6c21595351a8b4447ca09133346b49\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Man Asian Literary Prize 2011 winner\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_5fac59dd524a44b7b79f0283"},{"content":"I found a key clue. The Murakami page (e1) confirms: Murakami was born in **Fushimi-ku, Kyoto, Japan** and \"Growing up in Ashiya, near Kobe.\" His work is translated into 50 languages. Now I need to verify the Man Asian Literary Prize connection. Let me search for the prize winners and Murakami's specific book that was a contender.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Man Asian Literary Prize 2011 longlist Murakami 1Q84\", \"Man Asian Literary Prize 2012 winner\", \"Man Asian Literary Prize 2013 winner\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_cb5f3583aacf4e8987c1b9e2","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Man Asian Literary Prize Wikipedia winners list\", \"Man Asian Literary Prize 2011 2012 2013 shortlist\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_b7775c4dc6dd443cadaaeb00","index":1,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e1\",\"start\":0}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d74\"},\"ref\":\"d74\",\"snippet\":\" ... Shinchosha Publishing published Murakami's novel 1Q84 in Japan on May 29, 2009. 1Q84 is pronounced \\\"ichi kyū hachi yon\\\", the same as 1984, as 9 is also pronounced \\\"kyū\\\" in Japanese. The book was longlisted for the Man Asian Literary Prize in 2011. However, after the 2012 ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haruki_Murakami\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d83\"},\"ref\":\"d83\",\"snippet\":\" ... an Ending (2011), Jesmyn Ward, Salvage the Bones (2011), Haruki Murakami, 1Q84 (first English translation, 2011), Ernest Cline, Ready Player One (2011), E. L. James, Fifty Shades of Grey (2011), Ben Lerner, Leaving the Atocha Station (2011), Karen Russell, Swamplandia! (2011), Tom Perrotta, The Leftovers (2011), Maria Semple ... \",\"title\":\"https://lithub.com/a-century-of-reading-the-10-books-that-have-defined-the-2010s-so-far/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d48\"},\"ref\":\"d48\",\"snippet\":\" ... His collection Killdeer won the 2011 Governor General's Literary Award for poetry and the 2012 Trillium Book Award. It was also shortlisted for the 2012 Griffin Poetry Prize. His other collections include Trouble Sleeping, An Oak Hunch, The Small Nouns Crying Faith and Notes from Gethsemani.\\n\\neat ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.cbc.ca/books/37-canadian-poetry-collections-to-watch-for-in-fall-2020-1.5716100\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d84\"},\"ref\":\"d84\",\"snippet\":\" ... Throughout his career, Murakami has received numerous literary awards and honors, including the World Fantasy Award, the Franz Kafka Prize, and the Jerusalem Prize. His work has been adapted into films, plays, and other media. Despite his global popularity, Murakami remains a somewhat controversial figure in Japan, where ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.audible.com/blog/summary-the-city-and-its-uncertain-walls-by-haruki-murakami\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d85\"},\"ref\":\"d85\",\"snippet\":\" ... LOL\\n\\n1Q84 was one of the weirdest books I've ever read, but it was so oddly compelling–I couldn't put it down. I also want to read Murakami's The Wind-Up Bird Chronicles.\\n\\nI gave up on The Elegance of the Hedgehog not very far ... \",\"title\":\"https://modernmrsdarcy.com/books-translation/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d86\"},\"ref\":\"d86\",\"snippet\":\" ... PEN Translation Prize\\ndate: 2025-01-01\\n---\\nThe PEN Translation Prize is an annual award for book-length prose translations from any language into English. Awarded annually since 1963, the award confers a $3,000 prize to the translator of the winning book.\\n\\nAll winners, finalists, and longlisters ... \",\"title\":\"https://pen.org/literary-awards/pen-translation-prize/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d87\"},\"ref\":\"d87\",\"snippet\":\" ... solidified her place in the pantheon of magical realist writers.\\n\\n-\\n\\n-\\n\\nHaruki Murakami:\\n\\n-\\n\\nHailing from Japan, Murakami is known for blending the ordinary with the surreal in his novels. Works such as \\\"Kafka on the Shore\\\" and \\\"1Q84\\\" showcase his mastery of magical realism, infusing contemporary settings with dreamlike ... \",\"title\":\"https://blueroseone.com/publish/magical-realism/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d6\"},\"ref\":\"d6\",\"snippet\":\" ... A Russian version of the Booker Prize was created in 1992 called the Booker-Open Russia Literary Prize, also known as the Russian Booker Prize. In 2007, Man Group plc established the Man Asian Literary Prize, an annual literary award given to the best novel by an Asian ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d88\"},\"ref\":\"d88\",\"snippet\":\" ... Hartfield is, however, very clearly based upon Vonnegut's Kilgore Trout and is likely used as a reference to another of Mu